Task title: Queue (Java)
Task description:
Implement a class "Queue" that works like a queue (as described in the
the lecture). The class should have at least the
methods emptyqueue(), head(), enqueue(x) and dequeue(). The
queue does not need to hold more than 100 elements.

Note 1: In the Java test, the stack is expected to store "strings".
Since Python is dynamically typed, this does not apply.

Note 2: It is not allowed to use "import"!

Student code currently passes 0/11 tests and fails 11/11 tests.

Student code:
```java
public class Queue {
    QueueItem head;
    QueueItem last;

    public Queue() {

    }


    public boolean emptyqueue() {
        return head == null;
    }

    public String head() {
        return head.value;
    }

    public void enqueue(String s) {
        if(head == null) {
            head = new QueueItem(s);
            last = head;
        } else {
            last.nextItem = new QueueItem(s);
            last = last.nextItem;
        }
    }

    public String dequeue() {
        String res = head.value;
        head = head.nextItem;
        return res;
    }
}

public class QueueItem {
    QueueItem nextItem;
    String value;

    public QueueItem(String value) {
        this.value = value;
    }
}

