Task title: Search trees: Removal (Java)
Task description:
These tasks will again be about search trees. Reminder:
Our search trees are built from "nodes", analogous to the lecture.
A node looks like this:

public class Node {
    public int key;
    public Node left;
    public Node right;
    public Node parent;
}

For this task, implement a method "delete" which deletes a
"Node" in the search tree and returns the new search tree. Use the
the method from the lecture slides, i.e. the one with "TREE-MINIMUM".
The nodes can be reused as desired. The function gets the root
of the search tree and the node to be deleted.


Student code currently passes 9/10 tests and fails 1/10 tests.

Student code:
```java
// Node in parameter represents root of tree
/*
Implementieren Sie für diese Aufgabe eine Methode "delete", die eine "Node" 
im Suchbaum löscht und den neuen Suchbaum zurück gibt.

Methode nutzbar: TREE-MINIMUM(Node x)
*/
public Node delete(Node root, Node delete) {
    Node y;
    if (delete.left == null || delete.right == null) {
        y = delete;
    }
    else {
        Node k = delete.right;
        while (k.left != null) k = k.left;
        y = k;
    }

    Node x;
    if (y.left != null) {
        x = y.left;
    }
    else {
        x = y.right;
    }

    //boolean rootChanged = false;
    if (x != null) x.parent = y.parent;
    if (y.parent == null) {
        y = null;
        delete = null;
        return null;
        //x.parent = null; //root, vorsicht!
    }
    else {
        if (y == y.parent.left) {
            y.parent.left = x;
        }
        else {
            y.parent.right = x;
        }
    }

    if (y != delete) delete.key = y.key;
    y.parent = null;
    y.left = null;
    y.right = null;
    y = null;

    return root;
}

